From: rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] ath10k: allow raw TX on monitor vdev without global raw mode

On WCN3990 (ath10k_snoc) the firmware does not advertise
ATH10K_FW_FEATURE_RAW_MODE_SUPPORT in the firmware-5.bin feature flags,
so ATH10K_FLAG_RAW_MODE is never set and ath10k_mac_tx() silently drops
every frame sent through a monitor interface (the WARN_ON_ONCE + free path).

The bit gating injection was always a host-driver-side guard, not a
firmware limitation.  qcacld-3.0 (Qualcomm's downstream driver for the
same chip and the same wlanmdsp.mbn) has no equivalent check and performs
raw TX without issue.

This patch takes the minimal surgical approach: if the frame is being
sent through a monitor vdev (NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR), skip the global
raw-mode flag check and let the HTT raw TX descriptor through.  Normal
STA/AP traffic is unaffected; rx_decap_mode stays at NATIVE_WIFI.

The companion change is patching firmware-5.bin to set bit 10
(ATH10K_FW_FEATURE_RAW_MODE_SUPPORT) so that the driver correctly
advertises raw-mode support when the ath10k_core module is loaded with
frame_mode=0.  Without the kernel change, frame_mode=0 still requires
the global flag for non-monitor TX paths.

On-device usage after applying both changes:
  ip link set wlan0 down
  iw dev wlan0 set type monitor
  iw reg set 00
  ip link set wlan0 up
  iw dev wlan0 set channel 6
  # passive RX:  tcpdump -i wlan0 --immediate-mode
  # TX injection: aireplay-ng / scapy / mdk4 on wlan0

Signed-off-by: rhodep port <rhodep@postmarketos>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
@@ -4084,8 +4084,12 @@ static int ath10k_mac_tx(struct ath10k *ar,
 	case ATH10K_HW_TXRX_RAW:
 		if (!test_bit(ATH10K_FLAG_RAW_MODE, &ar->dev_flags) &&
-		    !(skb_cb->flags & ATH10K_SKB_F_RAW_TX)) {
+		    !(skb_cb->flags & ATH10K_SKB_F_RAW_TX) &&
+		    !(vif && vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR)) {
 			WARN_ON_ONCE(1);
 			ieee80211_free_txskb(hw, skb);
 			return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 		}
+		/* Monitor vif: frame is a raw 802.11 frame from userspace
+		 * (aireplay-ng / scapy / mdk4).  Let the HTT raw TX
+		 * descriptor reach the firmware without a global raw-mode flag. */
 		break;
 	}
